WEBVTT

00:00:05.933 --> 00:00:07.744
Previously on Supernatural.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:14.101
Take your brother outside as
fast as you can! Now Dean! Go!

00:00:15.446 --> 00:00:17.024
Mary! No!

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:19.923
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:21.048 --> 00:00:22.599
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:24.565 --> 00:00:25.964
I swore I was done hunting,

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.146
I can't do this alone.

00:00:33.785 --> 00:00:35.089
We got work to do.

00:00:35.459 --> 00:00:36.722
This is dad's single

00:00:36.763 --> 00:00:38.039
Most valuable possession.

00:00:38.066 --> 00:00:40.371
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:40.413 --> 00:00:42.380
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:42.421 --> 00:00:43.724
You know, saving people,

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:44.836
Hunting things...

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:45.755
Family business.

00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:46.283
No.

00:00:46.324 --> 00:00:47.696
I gotta find Jessica's killer.

00:00:47.737 --> 00:00:49.206
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.108
Sam, you know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:00:52.917 --> 00:00:54.310
Yeah, I know.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:10.740
Morning, daddy.

00:01:10.802 --> 00:01:12.179
Morning, sweetheart.

00:01:14.406 --> 00:01:16.674
All these workouts, Soph, I don't know.

00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:18.599
Guys don't like buff girls.

00:01:18.693 --> 00:01:21.561
Yeah, well, girls don't like
guys who still live at home.

00:01:28.465 --> 00:01:29.873
Be careful.

00:01:29.936 --> 00:01:31.031
I will.

00:03:07.337 --> 00:03:08.902
Can I get you anything else?

00:03:12.109 --> 00:03:13.674
Just the check, please.

00:03:13.772 --> 00:03:14.679
Okay.

00:03:19.452 --> 00:03:22.707
You know, Sam, we are allowed
to have fun once in a while.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.634
That's fun.

00:03:30.972 --> 00:03:32.990
Here, take a look at
this. I think I got one.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.930
Lake Manitoc, Wisconsin.

00:03:35.102 --> 00:03:36.729
Last week, Sophie Carlton,

00:03:36.828 --> 00:03:39.049
18, walks into the lake,

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.317
Doesn't walk out.

00:03:40.364 --> 00:03:42.038
Authorities dragged the water.

00:03:42.116 --> 00:03:43.008
Nothing.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:46.048
Sophie Carlton is the third
Lake Manitoc drowning this year.

00:03:46.173 --> 00:03:47.941
None of the other
bodies were found, either

00:03:48.082 --> 00:03:49.224
They had a funeral two days ago.

00:03:49.286 --> 00:03:49.897
A funeral?

00:03:49.943 --> 00:03:51.977
Yes, they buried an empty coffin.

00:03:52.235 --> 00:03:55.114
For closure or whatever.

00:03:55.349 --> 00:03:56.428
Closure?

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.508
What closure?

00:03:58.712 --> 00:04:00.480
People don't just disappear, Dean.

00:04:00.714 --> 00:04:02.670
Other people just stop looking for them.

00:04:04.458 --> 00:04:05.553
Something you want to say to me?

00:04:05.589 --> 00:04:08.327
The trail for dad. It's getting colder.

00:04:08.452 --> 00:04:09.031
Every day.

00:04:09.062 --> 00:04:11.080
What are we supposed
to do? I don't know.

00:04:11.299 --> 00:04:12.128
Something.

00:04:12.269 --> 00:04:13.411
Anything. No one.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.840
I'm sick of this attitude.

00:04:15.168 --> 00:04:16.749
You don't think I want to
find dad as much as you do?

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:17.562
Yeah, I know you do it.

00:04:17.593 --> 00:04:20.269
I'm the one that's been with him every
single day for the past two years.

00:04:20.378 --> 00:04:22.569
While you've been off to
college going to pep rallies.

00:04:22.709 --> 00:04:23.898
We will find dad,

00:04:23.961 --> 00:04:26.167
But until then, we're
gonna kill everything bad,

00:04:26.307 --> 00:04:27.841
Between here and there.

00:04:28.654 --> 00:04:29.703
Okay?

00:04:36.361 --> 00:04:38.332
All right, Lake Manitoc.

00:04:39.036 --> 00:04:39.411
Hey.

00:04:39.521 --> 00:04:39.959
Huh?

00:04:40.006 --> 00:04:40.804
How far?

00:05:02.103 --> 00:05:02.963
Will Carlton?

00:05:03.339 --> 00:05:04.027
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:04.183 --> 00:05:05.247
I'm agent Ford.

00:05:05.428 --> 00:05:06.773
This is agent Hamill.

00:05:07.258 --> 00:05:09.042
We're with the U.S. Wildlife service.

00:05:16.344 --> 00:05:18.221
She was about 100 yards out.

00:05:19.848 --> 00:05:20.943
That's where she got dragged down.

00:05:21.006 --> 00:05:22.351
And you're sure she didn't just drown?

00:05:22.383 --> 00:05:22.821
Yeah.

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:24.573
She was a varsity swimmer.

00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:26.450
She practically grew up in that lake.

00:05:27.576 --> 00:05:29.751
She's as safe out there
as in her own bathtub.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.597
So no splashing,

00:05:31.691 --> 00:05:32.802
No signs of distress?

00:05:32.849 --> 00:05:34.006
No, that's what I'm telling you.

00:05:34.183 --> 00:05:36.326
Did you see any shadows in the water,

00:05:37.171 --> 00:05:38.016
Maybe,

00:05:38.219 --> 00:05:40.659
Some dark shape breach the surface?

00:05:40.706 --> 00:05:42.724
No, again, she was really far out there.

00:05:42.818 --> 00:05:44.570
You ever see any strange
tracks by the shoreline?

00:05:44.601 --> 00:05:45.509
No, never.

00:05:45.618 --> 00:05:46.432
Why?

00:05:46.557 --> 00:05:47.903
What do you think's out there?

00:05:48.357 --> 00:05:50.641
We'll let you know as soon as we do.

00:05:52.878 --> 00:05:54.380
What about your father?

00:05:54.615 --> 00:05:56.070
Can we talk to him?

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:58.782
Look.

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.377
If you don't mind, I mean,

00:06:00.581 --> 00:06:03.100
He didn't see anything, and
he's kind of been through a lot.

00:06:03.991 --> 00:06:05.243
We understand.

00:06:11.598 --> 00:06:12.542
Now, I'm sorry, but,

00:06:12.568 --> 00:06:16.767
Why does the wildlife service
care about an accidental drowning?

00:06:16.902 --> 00:06:18.247
You sure it's accidental?

00:06:18.503 --> 00:06:20.489
Will Carlton saw
something grab his sister.

00:06:21.053 --> 00:06:22.195
Like what?

00:06:22.633 --> 00:06:23.665
Here, sit, please.

00:06:23.712 --> 00:06:26.748
There are no indigenous
carnivores in that lake.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:29.642
There's nothing even big
enough to pull down a person,

00:06:29.728 --> 00:06:31.574
Unless it was the Loch Ness monster.

00:06:32.427 --> 00:06:33.882
Yeah, right.

00:06:34.007 --> 00:06:38.075
Will Carlton was traumatized, and
sometimes the mind plays tricks.

00:06:38.502 --> 00:06:39.362
Still,

00:06:39.894 --> 00:06:43.461
We dragged that entire lake.
We even ran a sonar sweep,

00:06:43.889 --> 00:06:46.282
Just to be sure, and there
was nothing down there.

00:06:46.361 --> 00:06:48.410
That's weird, though.

00:06:48.817 --> 00:06:50.444
That's the third missing body this year.

00:06:50.527 --> 00:06:51.622
I know.

00:06:52.279 --> 00:06:54.063
These are people from my town.

00:06:54.251 --> 00:06:55.721
These are people I care about.

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:56.644
I know.

00:06:58.026 --> 00:06:59.074
Anyway . . .

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:02.031
All this.

00:07:03.361 --> 00:07:05.239
It won't be a problem much longer.

00:07:05.817 --> 00:07:06.866
What do you mean?

00:07:07.654 --> 00:07:09.188
Well, the dam, of course.

00:07:10.502 --> 00:07:11.691
Of course.

00:07:11.957 --> 00:07:12.864
The dam.

00:07:13.177 --> 00:07:14.210
It's, uh...

00:07:15.649 --> 00:07:16.494
It sprung a leak.

00:07:16.572 --> 00:07:17.699
It's falling apart,

00:07:18.309 --> 00:07:21.067
And the feds won't give
us the grant to repair it,

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:22.820
So they've opened the spillway.

00:07:23.445 --> 00:07:25.229
In another six months,

00:07:25.839 --> 00:07:27.263
There won't be much of a lake.

00:07:27.513 --> 00:07:29.082
There won't be much of a town, either,

00:07:29.223 --> 00:07:30.287
But as federal wildlife,

00:07:30.412 --> 00:07:31.805
You already knew that.

00:07:32.509 --> 00:07:33.338
Exactly.

00:07:33.995 --> 00:07:35.935
Sorry, am I interrupting?

00:07:36.472 --> 00:07:37.692
I think come back later.

00:07:37.833 --> 00:07:39.835
Gentlemen, this is my daughter.

00:07:40.258 --> 00:07:41.447
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:41.791 --> 00:07:42.714
I'm Dean.

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:44.482
Andrea Bar. Hi.

00:07:44.686 --> 00:07:45.108
Hi.

00:07:45.332 --> 00:07:46.849
They're from the wildlife service,

00:07:47.459 --> 00:07:48.711
About the lake.

00:07:52.878 --> 00:07:54.208
Oh, hey, there.

00:07:54.494 --> 00:07:55.448
What's your name?

00:08:01.769 --> 00:08:03.099
His name is Lucas.

00:08:05.974 --> 00:08:06.850
Is he okay?

00:08:06.928 --> 00:08:08.555
My grandson's been through a lot.

00:08:09.478 --> 00:08:10.793
We all have.

00:08:11.669 --> 00:08:12.482
Well,

00:08:13.254 --> 00:08:14.818
If there's anything
else I can do for you,

00:08:14.835 --> 00:08:15.899
Please, let me know.

00:08:16.023 --> 00:08:16.774
Thanks.

00:08:17.655 --> 00:08:19.360
You know, now that you mentioned it,

00:08:19.454 --> 00:08:22.693
Could you point us in the direction
of a reasonably priced motel?

00:08:22.885 --> 00:08:25.592
Lake front motel, go around
the corner, it's two blocks up.

00:08:25.655 --> 00:08:26.374
Two.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.001
Would you mind showing us?

00:08:29.394 --> 00:08:31.068
You want me to walk you two blocks?

00:08:31.146 --> 00:08:32.429
Not if it's any trouble.

00:08:33.038 --> 00:08:34.900
I'm headed that way anyway.

00:08:36.042 --> 00:08:38.092
I'll be back to pick up lucas at 3:00.

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:39.922
We'll go to the park, okay, sweetie?

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:44.981
Thanks again.

00:08:46.045 --> 00:08:47.265
So, cute kid.

00:08:47.625 --> 00:08:48.204
Thanks.

00:08:50.353 --> 00:08:51.824
Kids are the best, huh?

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:56.960
There it is.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:59.072
Like I said, two blocks.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:08:59.917
Thanks.

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:03.171
Must be hard with your
sense of direction,

00:09:03.547 --> 00:09:06.441
Never being able to find your
way to a decent pickup line.

00:09:07.979 --> 00:09:09.215
Enjoy your stay.

00:09:11.077 --> 00:09:12.204
"Kids are the best"?

00:09:12.803 --> 00:09:14.649
You don't even like kids. I love kids.

00:09:14.712 --> 00:09:16.949
Name three children that you even know.

00:09:23.676 --> 00:09:24.740
I'm thinking.

00:09:25.147 --> 00:09:27.650
So there's the three
drowning victims this year.

00:09:27.681 --> 00:09:28.620
And before that?

00:09:28.761 --> 00:09:31.530
Yeah, six more,

00:09:31.561 --> 00:09:33.141
Spread outover the past 35 years.

00:09:33.282 --> 00:09:35.081
Those bodies were
never recovered, either.

00:09:35.691 --> 00:09:37.178
If there is something out there,

00:09:37.328 --> 00:09:38.283
It's picking up its pace.

00:09:38.345 --> 00:09:39.863
So we got a lake monster on a binge?

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:42.601
This whole lake monster
theory, it just bugs me.

00:09:42.867 --> 00:09:43.712
Why?

00:09:44.249 --> 00:09:46.001
Loch Ness, lake Champlain

00:09:46.032 --> 00:09:48.598
There are literally hundreds
of eyewitness accounts,

00:09:48.645 --> 00:09:50.507
But here, almost nothing.

00:09:50.835 --> 00:09:52.115
Whatever it is out there,

00:09:52.416 --> 00:09:53.777
Noone's living to talk about it.

00:09:54.028 --> 00:09:55.295
Wait, Bar,

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:57.428
Christopher Bar, where have
I heard that name before?

00:09:57.459 --> 00:10:00.072
Christopher Bar, the victim in may.

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:03.639
Christopher Bar was Andrea's husband,

00:10:03.934 --> 00:10:05.373
Lucas' father.

00:10:05.831 --> 00:10:06.708
Apparently,

00:10:06.942 --> 00:10:08.773
He took Lucas out swimming.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:12.246
Lucas was on a floating wooden
platform when Chris drowned,

00:10:12.543 --> 00:10:13.685
Two hours,

00:10:14.124 --> 00:10:15.970
Before the kid got rescued.

00:10:19.677 --> 00:10:21.711
Maybe we have an eyewitness after all.

00:10:22.196 --> 00:10:24.011
No wonder that kid was so freaked out.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:27.958
Watching one of your parents die
isn't something you just get over.

00:10:30.133 --> 00:10:31.385
Can we join you?

00:10:35.377 --> 00:10:36.801
I'm here with my son.

00:10:40.196 --> 00:10:41.432
Mind if I say hi?

00:10:43.786 --> 00:10:47.212
Tell your friend this whole "jerry
maguire" thing's not gonna work on me.

00:10:48.026 --> 00:10:49.700
I don't think that's what this is about.

00:10:52.991 --> 00:10:54.133
How's it going?

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:03.826
Oh, I used to love these things.

00:11:10.495 --> 00:11:12.451
So crayons is more your thing?

00:11:12.983 --> 00:11:14.970
That's cool. Chicks dig artists.

00:11:17.425 --> 00:11:18.786
Hey, these are pretty good.

00:11:20.366 --> 00:11:22.431
You mind if I sit and
draw with you for a while?

00:11:22.874 --> 00:11:24.454
I'm not so bad myself.

00:11:33.964 --> 00:11:35.826
You know, I'm thinking you can hear me.

00:11:36.373 --> 00:11:37.797
You just don't want to talk.

00:11:38.345 --> 00:11:40.535
I don't know exactly
what happened to your dad,

00:11:41.637 --> 00:11:43.501
But I know it was something real bad.

00:11:47.005 --> 00:11:48.585
I think I know how you feel.

00:11:51.041 --> 00:11:53.325
When I was your age, I saw something.

00:12:00.208 --> 00:12:01.397
Anyway . . .

00:12:03.404 --> 00:12:06.221
Maybe you don't think
anyone will listen to you.

00:12:06.961 --> 00:12:07.947
Or, uh...

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:10.963
Or believe you.

00:12:11.573 --> 00:12:13.341
I want you to know that I will.

00:12:14.749 --> 00:12:16.266
You don't even have to

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:18.331
Say anything. You
could draw me a picture,

00:12:18.394 --> 00:12:19.740
About what you saw that day,

00:12:20.038 --> 00:12:21.274
With your dad,

00:12:22.572 --> 00:12:23.433
On the lake.

00:12:27.517 --> 00:12:28.425
Okay,

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:29.535
No problem.

00:12:30.005 --> 00:12:31.022
This is for you.

00:12:32.148 --> 00:12:33.462
This is my family.

00:12:34.761 --> 00:12:35.997
That's my dad.

00:12:36.362 --> 00:12:37.206
That's...

00:12:38.912 --> 00:12:39.944
That's my mom.

00:12:40.715 --> 00:12:42.311
That's my geek brother,

00:12:43.203 --> 00:12:44.392
And that's me.

00:12:48.288 --> 00:12:49.977
All right, so I'm a sucky artist.

00:12:50.404 --> 00:12:51.765
I'll see you around, Lucas.

00:13:04.971 --> 00:13:07.912
Lucas hasn't said a
word, not even to me,

00:13:08.527 --> 00:13:09.623
Not since

00:13:10.577 --> 00:13:12.157
His dad's accident.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:13.972
Yeah, we heard.

00:13:14.254 --> 00:13:15.177
Sorry.

00:13:16.303 --> 00:13:18.102
What are the doctors saying?

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:20.879
That it's a kind of
post-Traumatic stress.

00:13:20.973 --> 00:13:22.194
That can't be easy

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:23.054
For either of you.

00:13:23.117 --> 00:13:24.619
We moved in with my dad.

00:13:25.589 --> 00:13:27.247
He helps out a lot.

00:13:29.242 --> 00:13:30.384
It's just...

00:13:31.964 --> 00:13:35.312
When I think about what Lucas
went through, what he saw...

00:13:37.659 --> 00:13:38.926
Kids are strong.

00:13:39.486 --> 00:13:41.504
You'd be surprised
what they can deal with.

00:13:42.302 --> 00:13:43.366
You know,

00:13:43.883 --> 00:13:45.494
He used to have such life.

00:13:45.776 --> 00:13:48.169
He was hard to keep up
with, to tell you the truth.

00:13:49.369 --> 00:13:50.761
Now he just sits there,

00:13:50.871 --> 00:13:53.483
Drawing those pictures,
playing with those army men.

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:55.022
I just wish.

00:13:55.710 --> 00:13:56.805
Hey, sweetie.

00:14:02.318 --> 00:14:03.100
Thanks.

00:14:04.132 --> 00:14:05.259
Thanks, Lucas.

00:14:23.375 --> 00:14:24.627
Hey, dad.

00:14:26.019 --> 00:14:27.834
You should probably eat something.

00:14:29.982 --> 00:14:31.547
I'm gonna make some dinner, okay?

00:16:26.125 --> 00:16:27.189
So,

00:16:27.299 --> 00:16:29.317
I think it's safe to say
we can rule out Nessie.

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:30.146
What do you mean?

00:16:30.229 --> 00:16:33.358
I just drove past the Carlton
house. There was an ambulance there.

00:16:33.561 --> 00:16:34.907
Will Carlton is dead.

00:16:35.141 --> 00:16:35.720
He drowned?

00:16:35.767 --> 00:16:37.379
Yep, in the sink.

00:16:38.098 --> 00:16:39.240
What the hell?

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:41.858
So this isn't a creature. We're
dealing with something else.

00:16:41.905 --> 00:16:42.687
Yeah, but what?

00:16:42.734 --> 00:16:43.344
I don't know.

00:16:43.469 --> 00:16:44.611
A water wraith maybe?

00:16:44.846 --> 00:16:45.925
Some kind of demon?

00:16:46.137 --> 00:16:47.811
I mean, something that controls water

00:16:50.242 --> 00:16:51.791
water that comes from the Same source.

00:16:51.854 --> 00:16:52.667
The lake Yeah

00:16:52.699 --> 00:16:54.607
Which would explain why
it's upping the body count.

00:16:54.983 --> 00:16:57.877
The lake is draining. It'll be dry in
a few months. Whatever this thing is,

00:16:57.949 --> 00:16:59.388
Whatever it wants,

00:16:59.717 --> 00:17:00.577
It's running out of time.

00:17:00.609 --> 00:17:02.158
And if it can get through the pipes,

00:17:02.596 --> 00:17:03.602
It can get to anyone,

00:17:03.665 --> 00:17:04.603
Almost anywhere.

00:17:04.697 --> 00:17:06.700
This is gonna happen again soon.

00:17:06.981 --> 00:17:08.483
And we do know one other thing for sure.

00:17:08.515 --> 00:17:10.815
We know this has got something
to do with Bill Carlton.

00:17:10.877 --> 00:17:11.901
It took both his kids.

00:17:11.948 --> 00:17:13.199
And I've been asking around.

00:17:13.324 --> 00:17:14.560
Lucas' dad, Chris

00:17:15.045 --> 00:17:16.328
Bill Carlton's godson.

00:17:17.001 --> 00:17:18.753
Let's go pay Mr. Carlton a visit.

00:17:21.265 --> 00:17:22.532
Mr. Carlton?

00:17:25.254 --> 00:17:27.272
We'd like to ask you a few questions,

00:17:27.351 --> 00:17:28.039
If you don't mind.

00:17:28.102 --> 00:17:30.495
We're from the department I
don't care who you're with.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.614
I've answered enough questions today.

00:17:35.694 --> 00:17:38.432
Your son said he saw
something in that lake.

00:17:39.402 --> 00:17:40.560
What about you?

00:17:41.098 --> 00:17:42.663
You ever see anything out there?

00:17:44.149 --> 00:17:45.119
Mr. Carlton,

00:17:45.150 --> 00:17:47.106
Sophie's drowning and Will's death.

00:17:47.403 --> 00:17:48.874
We think there might be a connection,

00:17:48.968 --> 00:17:51.862
To you or your family.
My children are gone.

00:17:55.447 --> 00:17:56.214
It's...

00:17:59.358 --> 00:18:01.032
It's worse than dying.

00:18:08.285 --> 00:18:09.318
Go away...

00:18:10.976 --> 00:18:11.852
Please.

00:18:14.845 --> 00:18:16.081
What do you think?

00:18:17.051 --> 00:18:19.053
I think the poor guy's
been through hell.

00:18:19.836 --> 00:18:21.650
I also think he's not
telling us something.

00:18:21.682 --> 00:18:22.699
So now what?

00:18:25.499 --> 00:18:26.406
What is it?

00:18:30.114 --> 00:18:32.727
Maybe Bill's not the only
one who knows something.

00:18:43.454 --> 00:18:45.237
I'm sorry, but I don't
think it's a good idea.

00:18:45.337 --> 00:18:46.432
I just need to talk to him,

00:18:46.495 --> 00:18:47.559
Just for a few minutes.

00:18:47.731 --> 00:18:49.342
He won't say anything.

00:18:49.827 --> 00:18:51.454
What good's it gonna do? Andrea,

00:18:51.658 --> 00:18:53.269
We think more people might get hurt.

00:18:54.807 --> 00:18:56.215
We think something's
happening out there.

00:18:56.324 --> 00:18:58.953
My husband, the others,
they just drowned.

00:18:59.375 --> 00:19:00.095
That's all.

00:19:00.142 --> 00:19:01.300
If that's what you really believe,

00:19:01.362 --> 00:19:02.129
Then we'll go,

00:19:02.415 --> 00:19:04.386
But if you think there's
even a possibility

00:19:04.699 --> 00:19:06.483
That something else
could be going on here,

00:19:08.079 --> 00:19:09.549
Please let me talk to your son.

00:19:24.968 --> 00:19:26.251
Hey, Lucas.

00:19:27.773 --> 00:19:28.900
You remember me?

00:19:38.156 --> 00:19:39.705
You know, I, uh...

00:19:41.473 --> 00:19:43.773
I wanted to thank you
for that last drawing

00:19:46.928 --> 00:19:48.586
but the thing is

00:19:49.071 --> 00:19:50.448
I need your help again.

00:20:03.418 --> 00:20:05.061
How did you know to draw this?

00:20:08.038 --> 00:20:10.150
Did you know something
bad was gonna happen?

00:20:12.247 --> 00:20:13.295
Maybe you could

00:20:13.717 --> 00:20:15.250
Nod yes or no

00:20:15.344 --> 00:20:16.173
For me.

00:20:18.645 --> 00:20:19.693
You're scared.

00:20:24.869 --> 00:20:25.730
It's okay.

00:20:26.559 --> 00:20:27.732
I understand.

00:20:28.249 --> 00:20:29.610
See, when I was your age,

00:20:29.688 --> 00:20:32.176
I saw something real
bad happen to my mom,

00:20:34.934 --> 00:20:36.326
And I was scared, too.

00:20:39.116 --> 00:20:40.524
I didn't feel like talking,

00:20:40.915 --> 00:20:42.057
Just like you,

00:20:43.246 --> 00:20:44.795
But, see, my mom,

00:20:47.204 --> 00:20:49.269
I know she wanted me to be brave.

00:20:52.591 --> 00:20:54.249
I think about that every day.

00:20:59.431 --> 00:21:01.418
And I do my best to be brave.

00:21:05.397 --> 00:21:07.003
And maybe your dad

00:21:09.111 --> 00:21:10.707
Wants you to be brave, too.

00:21:32.668 --> 00:21:33.826
Thanks, Lucas.

00:21:38.696 --> 00:21:41.136
Andrea said the kid never drew
like that till his dad died.

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:44.547
There are cases going
through a traumatic experience

00:21:44.735 --> 00:21:49.386
Could make certain people more sensitive
to premonitions, psychic tendencies.

00:21:49.397 --> 00:21:51.767
What if Lucas is
tapping into it somehow?

00:21:52.059 --> 00:21:54.030
It's only a matter of time
before somebody else drowns,

00:21:54.044 --> 00:21:55.702
So if you got a better lead, please.

00:21:56.458 --> 00:21:57.460
All right.

00:21:57.699 --> 00:21:58.654
We got another house to find.

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:02.096
There's about a thousand yellow
two-Stories in this county alone.

00:22:02.722 --> 00:22:03.927
See this church?

00:22:04.381 --> 00:22:06.415
I bet there's less than a
thousand of those around here.

00:22:07.218 --> 00:22:10.002
Oh, college boy thinks he's so smart.

00:22:17.363 --> 00:22:18.709
You know, um...

00:22:20.570 --> 00:22:21.947
What you said about mom.

00:22:24.951 --> 00:22:26.703
You never told me that before.

00:22:27.251 --> 00:22:28.503
It's no big deal.

00:22:32.669 --> 00:22:35.219
Oh, god, we're not gonna have
to hug or anything, are we?

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:03.263
We're sorry to bother you, ma'am,

00:23:03.325 --> 00:23:05.735
But does a little boy
live here by chance?

00:23:05.876 --> 00:23:06.877
He might wear

00:23:07.002 --> 00:23:08.082
A blue ball cap,

00:23:08.348 --> 00:23:09.709
Has a red bicycle.

00:23:10.578 --> 00:23:11.626
No, sir.

00:23:13.081 --> 00:23:15.349
Not for a very long time.

00:23:16.898 --> 00:23:19.652
Peter's been gone 35 years now.

00:23:22.591 --> 00:23:24.297
The police never

00:23:25.454 --> 00:23:28.255
I never had any idea what happened.

00:23:31.464 --> 00:23:33.483
He just disappeared.

00:23:34.161 --> 00:23:35.522
Losing him,

00:23:37.697 --> 00:23:38.635
You know,

00:23:40.129 --> 00:23:40.708
It's...

00:23:42.841 --> 00:23:44.702
It's worse than dying.

00:23:49.729 --> 00:23:51.482
Did he disappear from here,

00:23:51.544 --> 00:23:52.530
I mean, from this house?

00:23:52.608 --> 00:23:53.813
He was supposed to

00:23:54.658 --> 00:23:55.784
Ride his bike

00:23:56.050 --> 00:23:57.208
Straight home

00:23:57.302 --> 00:23:58.412
After school,

00:23:58.835 --> 00:24:00.352
And he never showed up.

00:24:17.326 --> 00:24:19.250
"Peter Sweeney and Billy Carlton,

00:24:19.521 --> 00:24:20.976
1970."

00:24:26.723 --> 00:24:28.053
You've taken everything,

00:24:30.572 --> 00:24:31.824
Everyone.

00:24:34.785 --> 00:24:36.084
I've got nothing left.

00:24:39.541 --> 00:24:41.012
I didn't understand.

00:24:43.191 --> 00:24:44.490
I didn't believe.

00:24:47.353 --> 00:24:48.698
Now I think I do.

00:24:51.098 --> 00:24:53.147
I think I finally know what you want.

00:24:58.221 --> 00:25:00.427
Okay, this little boy,
Peter Sweeney, vanishes,

00:25:00.474 --> 00:25:02.820
And this is all connected
to Bill Carlton somehow.

00:25:02.852 --> 00:25:04.776
Bill sure as hell seems
to be hiding something.

00:25:04.839 --> 00:25:06.262
And Bill, the people he loves

00:25:06.408 --> 00:25:07.253
They're all getting punished.

00:25:07.457 --> 00:25:08.865
So that Bill did something to Peter.

00:25:09.084 --> 00:25:10.210
What if Bill killed him?

00:25:10.711 --> 00:25:12.056
Peter's spirit would be furious.

00:25:12.135 --> 00:25:13.574
It'd want revenge. It's possible.

00:25:18.988 --> 00:25:20.537
Mr. Carlton!

00:25:23.666 --> 00:25:25.089
Hey. Check it out.

00:25:32.989 --> 00:25:35.148
Mr. Carlton! You need to come back!

00:25:36.353 --> 00:25:38.559
Come out of the water !
Turn the boat around!

00:25:52.364 --> 00:25:53.881
Baby, what's wrong?

00:25:57.011 --> 00:25:58.575
Sam, Dean.

00:25:59.394 --> 00:26:01.287
I didn't expect to see you here.

00:26:02.273 --> 00:26:04.181
So now you're on a first-Name basis.

00:26:05.308 --> 00:26:06.450
What are you doing here?

00:26:06.502 --> 00:26:07.706
I brought you dinner.

00:26:08.051 --> 00:26:10.961
I'm sorry, sweetheart. I
don't really have the time.

00:26:15.081 --> 00:26:16.786
I heard about Bill Carlton.

00:26:17.083 --> 00:26:19.446
Is it true? Is something
going on with the lake?

00:26:21.417 --> 00:26:23.185
Right now, we don't
know what the truth is,

00:26:23.451 --> 00:26:25.939
But I think it might be better
if you and lucas went on home.

00:26:28.874 --> 00:26:30.595
Lucas, hey, what is it?

00:26:30.845 --> 00:26:32.238
Lucas. Lucas.

00:26:32.488 --> 00:26:34.882
Lucas, it's okay. It's okay. Hey,

00:26:34.960 --> 00:26:37.404
Lucas, it's okay. It's okay.

00:26:59.856 --> 00:27:02.985
Okay, just so I'm clear, you see . . .

00:27:03.219 --> 00:27:04.142
Something

00:27:04.627 --> 00:27:06.161
Attack Bill's boat,

00:27:06.630 --> 00:27:07.835
Sending Bill,

00:27:09.238 --> 00:27:11.647
Who is a very good swimmer, by the way,

00:27:11.913 --> 00:27:13.196
Into the drink,

00:27:14.025 --> 00:27:15.746
And you never see him again?

00:27:18.107 --> 00:27:19.640
Yeah, that about sums it up.

00:27:19.687 --> 00:27:21.189
And I'm supposed to believe this,

00:27:21.236 --> 00:27:23.958
Even though I've already
sonar-Swept that entire lake

00:27:24.381 --> 00:27:26.665
And what you're describing is impossible

00:27:27.353 --> 00:27:29.652
And you're not really wildlife service?

00:27:30.939 --> 00:27:31.768
That's right,

00:27:32.018 --> 00:27:32.722
I checked.

00:27:33.004 --> 00:27:34.631
The department's never heard of you two.

00:27:35.137 --> 00:27:35.841
See?

00:27:35.935 --> 00:27:37.843
Now, we can explain that. Enough,

00:27:38.594 --> 00:27:39.674
Please.

00:27:40.816 --> 00:27:43.194
The only reason you're
breathing free air

00:27:43.449 --> 00:27:47.298
Is one of Bill's neighbors saw him
steering out that boat just before you did.

00:27:48.033 --> 00:27:48.691
So

00:27:48.925 --> 00:27:50.505
We have a couple of options here.

00:27:50.803 --> 00:27:52.988
I can arrest you for
impersonating government officials

00:27:53.004 --> 00:27:56.608
And hold you as material witnesses
to Bill Carlton's disappearance,

00:27:56.857 --> 00:27:57.670
Or

00:27:57.983 --> 00:28:00.799
We can chalk this all up to a bad day,

00:28:01.070 --> 00:28:02.525
You get into your car,

00:28:02.665 --> 00:28:05.548
You put this town in
your rearview mirror,

00:28:05.561 --> 00:28:08.704
And you don't ever darken my doorstep

00:28:08.762 --> 00:28:09.476
Again!

00:28:12.182 --> 00:28:13.746
Door number two sounds good.

00:28:13.997 --> 00:28:15.499
That's the one I'd pick.

00:28:30.428 --> 00:28:31.429
Baby...

00:28:33.267 --> 00:28:34.800
What are you doing up?

00:28:37.617 --> 00:28:39.353
Come on, let's go to bed.

00:29:00.668 --> 00:29:01.669
Green.

00:29:01.810 --> 00:29:02.498
What?

00:29:02.623 --> 00:29:04.016
Light's green.

00:29:11.295 --> 00:29:13.126
Ah, the interstate's the other way.

00:29:13.157 --> 00:29:13.767
I know.

00:29:38.056 --> 00:29:40.481
But, Dean, this job, I think it's over.

00:29:40.528 --> 00:29:41.372
I'm not so sure.

00:29:41.419 --> 00:29:44.439
If bill murdered Peter Sweeney
and Peter's spirit got its revenge,

00:29:44.595 --> 00:29:46.692
Case closed. The spirit
should be at rest.

00:29:46.737 --> 00:29:49.053
All right, so what if we take
off and this thing isn't done?

00:29:49.350 --> 00:29:51.374
What if we missed something?
What if more people get hurt?

00:29:51.452 --> 00:29:53.032
But why would you think that?

00:29:54.846 --> 00:29:56.520
Because Lucas was really scared.

00:29:56.786 --> 00:29:58.273
That's what this is about?

00:29:59.243 --> 00:30:01.574
I just don't want to leave
town till I know the kid's okay.

00:30:02.043 --> 00:30:03.029
Who are you,

00:30:03.138 --> 00:30:04.969
And what have you done with my brother?

00:30:07.346 --> 00:30:08.551
Shut up.

00:31:38.888 --> 00:31:40.343
Are you sure about this?

00:31:40.671 --> 00:31:41.970
It's pretty late, man.

00:31:45.291 --> 00:31:46.762
Lucas? Lucas!

00:31:49.703 --> 00:31:50.626
Lucas!

00:32:29.697 --> 00:32:30.761
Can you tell me?

00:32:32.893 --> 00:32:33.754
No

00:32:41.798 --> 00:32:43.503
It doesn't make any sense.

00:32:47.602 --> 00:32:49.135
I'm going crazy.

00:32:50.152 --> 00:32:51.671
No, you're not.

00:32:53.095 --> 00:32:54.269
Tell me what happened.

00:32:54.879 --> 00:32:55.818
Everything.

00:33:00.008 --> 00:33:01.134
I heard...

00:33:04.107 --> 00:33:05.844
I thought I heard...

00:33:08.152 --> 00:33:09.967
There was this voice.

00:33:10.483 --> 00:33:11.453
What did it say?

00:33:11.500 --> 00:33:12.345
It said

00:33:13.305 --> 00:33:15.558
It said, "come play with me."

00:33:23.550 --> 00:33:25.052
What's happening?

00:33:44.342 --> 00:33:46.157
Do you recognize the
kids in these pictures?

00:33:46.282 --> 00:33:47.033
What?

00:33:48.942 --> 00:33:49.834
No, I huh...

00:33:49.912 --> 00:33:53.025
I mean, except that's
my dad right there.

00:33:53.233 --> 00:33:54.594
He must have been about

00:33:55.204 --> 00:33:56.831
12 in these pictures.

00:33:58.460 --> 00:33:59.821
Chris Bar's drowning

00:34:00.102 --> 00:34:02.465
The connection wasn't to Bill
Carlton. It must have been to sheriff.

00:34:02.527 --> 00:34:03.982
Bill and the sheriff,

00:34:04.342 --> 00:34:05.954
They were both involved with Peter.

00:34:06.225 --> 00:34:07.252
What about Chris?

00:34:07.867 --> 00:34:10.026
My dad, what are you talking about?

00:34:10.261 --> 00:34:11.153
Lucas?

00:34:11.873 --> 00:34:13.202
Lucas, what is it?

00:34:19.509 --> 00:34:21.684
Lucas, honey?

00:34:33.441 --> 00:34:35.881
You and Lucas get back to the
house and stay there, okay?

00:35:00.183 --> 00:35:01.435
Peter's bike.

00:35:02.233 --> 00:35:03.281
Who are you?

00:35:06.676 --> 00:35:08.162
Put the gun down, Jake.

00:35:08.866 --> 00:35:10.341
How did you know that was there?

00:35:10.388 --> 00:35:11.233
What happened?

00:35:11.437 --> 00:35:12.985
You and Bill killed Peter,

00:35:13.330 --> 00:35:15.176
Drowned him in the lake,
and then buried the bike?

00:35:16.130 --> 00:35:17.851
You can't bury the truth, Jake.

00:35:19.030 --> 00:35:20.657
Nothing stays buried.

00:35:24.224 --> 00:35:25.726
Go to your room, sweetie.

00:35:27.009 --> 00:35:27.854
Now.

00:35:27.901 --> 00:35:30.172
Lock the door and wait
for me. Don't come out.

00:35:30.546 --> 00:35:31.907
I don't know what the
hell you're talking about.

00:35:31.929 --> 00:35:34.348
You and Bill killed Peter
Sweeney 35 years ago.

00:35:34.442 --> 00:35:35.360
That's what the hell I'm talking about.

00:35:35.365 --> 00:35:35.975
Dad

00:35:36.256 --> 00:35:38.337
And now you got one
seriously pissed-Off spirit.

00:35:38.384 --> 00:35:39.636
It's gonna take Andrea,

00:35:39.745 --> 00:35:40.527
Lucas,

00:35:40.827 --> 00:35:41.812
Everyone you love.

00:35:42.313 --> 00:35:43.393
It's gonna drown them,

00:35:43.799 --> 00:35:45.661
And it's gonna drag their
bodies god knows where.

00:35:45.958 --> 00:35:48.227
So you can feel the Same
pain Peter's mom felt.

00:35:49.088 --> 00:35:50.386
And then after that,

00:35:51.276 --> 00:35:52.325
It's gonna take you,

00:35:52.638 --> 00:35:54.359
And it's not gonna stop until it does.

00:35:55.250 --> 00:35:56.314
How do you know that?

00:35:56.424 --> 00:35:58.880
Because that's exactly
what it did to Bill Carlton.

00:35:58.927 --> 00:36:00.072
Listen to yourselves,

00:36:00.323 --> 00:36:00.933
Both of you.

00:36:00.995 --> 00:36:02.122
You're insane.

00:36:02.169 --> 00:36:04.359
I don't really give a rat's
ass what you think of us,

00:36:05.367 --> 00:36:07.010
But if we're gonna
bring down this spirit,

00:36:07.229 --> 00:36:08.778
We need to find the remains,

00:36:09.044 --> 00:36:09.857
Salt them,

00:36:09.998 --> 00:36:11.125
And burn them into dust.

00:36:11.328 --> 00:36:12.840
Tell me you buried Peter somewhere.

00:36:12.862 --> 00:36:14.593
Tell me you didn't just
let him go in the lake.

00:36:19.960 --> 00:36:22.651
Come play with me.

00:36:26.520 --> 00:36:27.083
Dad,

00:36:27.146 --> 00:36:28.178
Is any of this true?

00:36:28.209 --> 00:36:29.461
No. Don't listen to them.

00:36:29.487 --> 00:36:30.791
They're liars, and they're dangerous.

00:36:30.947 --> 00:36:32.574
Something tried to drown me.

00:36:33.122 --> 00:36:34.405
Chris died on that lake.

00:36:34.436 --> 00:36:35.578
Dad, look at me.

00:36:38.894 --> 00:36:39.566
Tell me you

00:36:39.629 --> 00:36:41.162
You didn't kill anyone.

00:36:51.050 --> 00:36:52.161
Oh, my god.

00:36:56.213 --> 00:36:57.709
Billy and I were at the lake.

00:37:00.791 --> 00:37:03.420
Peter was the smallest
one. We always bullied him,

00:37:03.952 --> 00:37:05.062
But this time...

00:37:06.319 --> 00:37:07.414
It got rough.

00:37:12.343 --> 00:37:13.985
We were holding his
head under the water.

00:37:14.882 --> 00:37:16.134
We didn't mean to,

00:37:16.963 --> 00:37:18.653
But we held him under too long,

00:37:18.778 --> 00:37:19.983
And he drowned.

00:37:26.975 --> 00:37:28.289
We let the body go,

00:37:29.009 --> 00:37:30.073
And it sank.

00:37:37.146 --> 00:37:38.382
Oh, Andrea.

00:37:41.485 --> 00:37:42.659
We were kids.

00:37:43.159 --> 00:37:44.051
We were so scared.

00:37:44.082 --> 00:37:45.099
It was a mistake,

00:37:45.115 --> 00:37:45.970
But, Andrea,

00:37:46.262 --> 00:37:48.671
To say that I have anything
to do with these drownings,

00:37:48.702 --> 00:37:49.829
With Chris,

00:37:50.251 --> 00:37:51.894
Because of some ghost

00:37:52.176 --> 00:37:53.725
It's not rational.

00:37:54.746 --> 00:37:56.013
All right, listen to me,

00:37:56.514 --> 00:37:57.468
All of you.

00:37:58.141 --> 00:37:59.643
We need to get you away from this lake

00:37:59.737 --> 00:38:01.379
As far as we can right now.

00:38:05.304 --> 00:38:05.882
Lucas!

00:38:09.705 --> 00:38:11.754
Come play with me.

00:38:12.662 --> 00:38:13.444
Lucas!

00:38:13.636 --> 00:38:16.327
Lucas! Stay where you are!

00:38:35.315 --> 00:38:36.410
Oh, my god!

00:38:39.883 --> 00:38:41.072
Andrea, stay there.

00:38:41.213 --> 00:38:42.293
No, Lucas!

00:38:42.345 --> 00:38:43.643
We'll get him. Stay on the dock.

00:38:49.929 --> 00:38:50.904
Lucas?

00:38:53.622 --> 00:38:54.420
Sam?

00:38:56.313 --> 00:38:57.862
Lucas, where are you?

00:39:02.138 --> 00:39:02.764
Peter,

00:39:02.936 --> 00:39:03.906
If you can hear me,

00:39:05.068 --> 00:39:06.006
Please, Peter,

00:39:06.038 --> 00:39:06.789
I'm sorry.

00:39:08.275 --> 00:39:09.104
I'm so... Dad, no!

00:39:09.151 --> 00:39:10.215
I'm so sorry.

00:39:10.716 --> 00:39:11.279
Peter.

00:39:11.514 --> 00:39:12.202
Lucas

00:39:12.499 --> 00:39:14.658
He's j... he's just a little boy.

00:39:15.367 --> 00:39:17.448
Please, it's not his fault. It's mine.

00:39:17.589 --> 00:39:18.762
Please take me!

00:39:19.763 --> 00:39:20.311
Jake,

00:39:20.373 --> 00:39:20.733
No!

00:39:22.032 --> 00:39:23.487
Listen, let it be over!

00:39:25.748 --> 00:39:26.436
Dad

00:39:27.268 --> 00:39:28.099
Daddy!

00:39:30.632 --> 00:39:31.492
No

00:39:41.486 --> 00:39:42.346
No...

00:40:22.737 --> 00:40:23.473
Look,

00:40:24.302 --> 00:40:25.679
We're not gonna save everybody.

00:40:28.312 --> 00:40:28.969
I know.

00:40:29.751 --> 00:40:30.502
Sam,

00:40:30.878 --> 00:40:31.566
Dean.

00:40:31.707 --> 00:40:32.473
Hey.

00:40:34.194 --> 00:40:35.352
We're glad we caught you.

00:40:35.790 --> 00:40:36.682
We just, um,

00:40:37.875 --> 00:40:39.377
We made you lunch for the road.

00:40:40.159 --> 00:40:42.897
Lucas insisted on making
the sandwiches himself.

00:40:44.372 --> 00:40:45.421
Can I give it to them now?

00:40:47.345 --> 00:40:47.955
Of course.

00:40:49.174 --> 00:40:50.989
Come on, Lucas, let's
load this in the car.

00:40:57.611 --> 00:40:58.549
How you holding up?

00:41:00.990 --> 00:41:03.916
It's just gonna take a long time to
sort through everything, you know?

00:41:07.863 --> 00:41:09.459
Andrea, I'm sorry.

00:41:11.054 --> 00:41:12.259
You saved my son.

00:41:14.043 --> 00:41:15.779
I can't ask for more than that.

00:41:19.454 --> 00:41:20.315
Dad loved me.

00:41:21.441 --> 00:41:22.693
He loved Lucas.

00:41:23.679 --> 00:41:24.680
No matter what he did,

00:41:24.701 --> 00:41:25.822
I just have to...

00:41:27.579 --> 00:41:28.628
Hold on to that.

00:41:34.825 --> 00:41:35.643
All right,

00:41:35.806 --> 00:41:37.277
If you're gonna be talking now,

00:41:37.572 --> 00:41:40.580
This is a very important phrase, so
I want you to repeat it one more time.

00:41:40.776 --> 00:41:41.730
Zeppelin rules!

00:41:41.734 --> 00:41:43.140
That's right. Up high.

00:41:46.826 --> 00:41:48.786
Take care of your mom, okay?

00:41:56.731 --> 00:41:58.268
Thank you.

00:42:03.444 --> 00:42:04.719
Sam, move your ass.

00:42:05.112 --> 00:42:07.172
We're gonna run out of
daylight before we hit the road.



